<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # What Is Sustainable Fashion? – Lesson # 4</h2>
<p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Sustainable Fashion</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> What Is Sustainable Fashion?</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop an argumentative paragraph on a familiar topic or issue. Interactive: Collaborate on a group argumentative paper.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write an argumentative essay on sustainable fashion practices, providing supporting evidence (e.g., "Eco-friendly fabrics, like organic cotton and bamboo, help reduce water usage and chemical pollution.")</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can contribute to a group paper on sustainable fashion trends (e.g., "By 2018, some fashion companies had already implemented recycling programs to reduce waste in their production processes.")</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can help organize group ideas on why retro fashion is popular (e.g., "They have unique styles and are affordable.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students individually write 3-5 sentences describing a recent fashion trend they've noticed or asking about sustainable fashion choices. For example: "How have fashion trends evolved from the past to today?" or "What do you think makes a fashion brand truly sustainable?" Teacher encourages the use of vocabulary like 'fashion,' 'trend,' 'style,' 'environment,' and adjectives like 'fashionable,' 'trendy,' 'sustainable,' 'eco-friendly.'</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing a short paragraph (2-3 sentences) comparing a past fashion trend with a present one, using the past continuous with present simple and target vocabulary. E.g., "In the early 2000s, people were wearing low-rise jeans, which often involved fast fashion production. Today, both flared and ripped jeans are in style, and many brands are trying to offer more sustainable designs. The teacher will also orally model the pronunciation of multisyllabic words like 'sustainability' and 'eco-friendly,' focusing on stress.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'sustainable fashion' mean? Can you give an example of an 'eco-friendly' material?" (Checks understanding of key vocabulary).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'people were wearing low-rise jeans,' am I talking about now or the past?" (Checks understanding of past continuous).</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 10 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario:</b> Students receive a short argumentative paragraph focusing on the importance of sustainable fashion practices. The paragraph integrates the target grammar (past perfect, future simple, past continuous with present simple) and vocabulary (e.g., 'sustainability,' 'eco-friendly,' 'recycle,' 'evolve,' 'predict,' 'industry').</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short argumentative paragraph (e.g., "Over the last decades, the fashion industry had adopted many fast fashion trends, leading to significant environmental impact. However, recently, more consumers are choosing eco-friendly materials and brands. Sustainable fashion will continue to evolve, and we must predict its future by supporting innovative designs that recycle materials and reduce waste. By using eco-friendly fabrics, fashion brands can reduce their carbon footprint, helping to protect the environment.")</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpret and express opinions and arguments in written form about social and environmental issues related to fashion.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Writing focus):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the paragraph and identify the main argument. They write down the topic sentence in their notebooks.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify and underline all instances of target vocabulary (e.g., 'sustainability,' 'eco-friendly,' 'evolve') and the target grammar structures (past continuous, past perfect, future simple) within the text.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students write a sentence summarizing one piece of supporting evidence provided in the paragraph.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 10 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Accuracy focus on Writing.</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using past continuous with present simple to compare trends, past perfect for completed actions, and future simple for predictions. Target vocabulary: nouns (fashion, trend, vintage, retro, collection, style, materials, sustainability, launch, industry, designs, environment, prediction), verbs (evolve, predict, adopt, reflect, discuss, shop, design, create, follow, introduce, showcase, wear, prefer, inspire, change, return, recycle), adjectives (sustainable, fashionable, trendy, eco-friendly, vintage, retro, stylish, innovative, unique, recycled).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> Students complete sentences with the correct form of verbs (past continuous, past perfect, future simple) and appropriate vocabulary. E.g., "In the 90s, most people ______ (wear) baggy jeans, but today, fitted styles _______ (gain) popularity." / "Before sustainable practices were common, many brands _______ (produce) clothes without considering the ________ (environment)." / "Fashion trends _______ (continue) to ______ (evolve) next decade."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Argumentative Sentence Expansion (Semi-controlled):</b> Students are given a topic sentence related to sustainable fashion (e.g., "Sustainable fashion is crucial for the future of our planet.") and must write 2-3 supporting sentences, incorporating at least one example of past perfect and one future simple prediction, and using 3-4 target vocabulary words (e.g., 'eco-friendly,' 'recycle,' 'impact,' 'evolve'). For instance, "By 2018, some fashion companies had already implemented recycling programs to reduce waste in their production processes."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Paragraph Structuring (Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students receive scrambled sentences related to an argument about retro fashion or eco-friendly materials. They must collaboratively rearrange them to form a logical argumentative paragraph. After organizing, they review each other's paragraphs for correct grammar and vocabulary usage, providing peer feedback on clarity and coherence. E.g., "By organizing group ideas on why retro fashion is popular, they can clearly see that 'They have unique styles and are affordable.'"</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 15 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Group Argumentative Paragraph Writing. Students work in groups of 3-4 to develop an argumentative paragraph (approx. 80-100 words) on a chosen aspect of sustainable fashion. The teacher provides two prompts:</p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt A: Argue why adopting eco-friendly fashion choices is essential for protecting our environment.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt B: Argue for the rise in popularity of vintage and retro styles as a sustainable fashion trend.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Groups must include a clear topic sentence, 2-3 supporting sentences with evidence (e.g., "Eco-friendly fabrics, like organic cotton and bamboo, help reduce water usage and chemical pollution."), and a concluding sentence. They are encouraged to use at least one example of each target grammar structure (past continuous/present simple, past perfect, future simple) and at least 5 target vocabulary words (e.g., 'sustainability,' 'eco-friendly,' 'recycle,' 'innovative,' 'design,' 'evolve').</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme:</b> The task directly addresses "What Is Sustainable Fashion?" by having students articulate arguments about its importance or specific trends within it, reflecting on language that represents values towards sustainability.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in written expression, collaborative interaction for idea organization, and successful completion of the argumentative writing task using the learned language content.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 10 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on group collaboration and a rubric for the written argumentative paragraph.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group submits their argumentative paragraph. The teacher collects these for review and feedback. Students also briefly present their paragraph to another group, explaining their main argument orally.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of the argumentative statement.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of relevant supporting evidence and examples.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate and accurate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'sustainable,' 'eco-friendly,' 'recycle,' 'evolve,' 'predict').</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of grammar structures (past continuous with present simple, past perfect, future simple).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Cohesion and coherence of the paragraph structure.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and contribution to the group paper.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I learned about writing an argument is..."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The most challenging part of writing our paragraph was..."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"We successfully used the grammar points (Past Continuous/Present Simple, Past Perfect, Future Simple) in our writing." (Yes/No/Partially)</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 7 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did collaborating on the argumentative paragraph help you organize your ideas and express your views on sustainable fashion?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific vocabulary or grammar structures did you find most useful for presenting your argument, and why?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspects of the writing activities worked well, and where did students struggle most with constructing their arguments or applying the target grammar?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Were the provided examples and prompts effective in guiding their argumentative writing? What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for similar writing tasks in the future, particularly regarding the complexity of arguments at B1.1?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will be able to expand on their argumentative paragraphs, perhaps by preparing a short presentation or a summary to share their findings and arguments on sustainable fashion with a wider audience, integrating all four skills.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] <br> [Time: 3 min]</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>